"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, led by Sarah Tan from the Analytics Department and introduced by Alex. The project kick-off was scheduled for June 15th with an initial phase one budget of $500,000. The executive board later approved a total budget of $2 million to cover research, development, and marketing. The team has expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, as well as specific additions like Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Strategic partnerships have been established, including a collaboration with TechInnovate for AI research. Significant progress has been made, including a breakthrough in predictive analytics and the successful completion of the testing phase. A detailed report on phase two progress will be shared on November 20th, and feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. The project also involves a partner, Zenith Innovations, whose onboarding session was scheduled for April 15th, 2023."
